From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:33:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: allow explicit non-coherent
 DMA

The J713 DCP controller and its piodma child declare dma-noncoherent to
keep the non-coherent DMA path they were qualified on when the CPU
reports LoC zero. Permit that standard property at both levels so the
J713 device tree validates.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(cherry picked from commit 6832149d632ffe97b7ed379dd40eefd610fb7ca0)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index 49d1144bdb..6c56f77873 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -70,6 +70,8 @@ properties:
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  dma-noncoherent: true
+
   resets:
     maxItems: 1
 
@@ -277,6 +279,7 @@ properties:
     properties:
       iommus:
         maxItems: 1
+      dma-noncoherent: true
       memory-region:
         minItems: 1
         maxItems: 64
